    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.	At least three training centers capcitated with facilities
2.	TOT provided for 35 experts and skill training provided for one thousand extension agents 
3.	60 regional experts trained on forest governance
4.	Forestry year book produced
5.	85,000ha of dry forests managed properly 
6.	15,000 jobs created primarily for women and youth
7.	3500 ha of land restored with community forests 
8.	Forest management plan prepared for 3 NFPAs
9.	two botanical gardens established
10.	Scientific study on trade-offs and systems dynamics delivered
11.	15 experts trained on urban green landscape design
12&#x2022;	1 national guideline prepared for integration of green facilities in city planning</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Three colleges such as Wondo Genet College of Forestry, Holeta Polytechnic College and Mertulemariam TVET have been capacitated through provision of different forest tools and equipment procured abroad via UNDP
2.TOT provided for 28 (5 women) experts at WGCF with 2 rounds which are 80% of the target number of trainee.
3. 60 regional experts trained on forest governance
4. Efforts to integrate the collection and publishing report of forestry related data to the annual CSA data collection and reporting routines have progressed very much. Questionnaires, Manuals and guidelines are developed and encoded in the CAPI system. 
5. 78,504ha of dry forest is mapped and demarcated for PFM scheme which is 92 % of the target dry forest management
6. New jobs are created for 10,856 (Female = 4,385) beneficiaries.
7. 19,248ha of community forest is demarcated for restoration through Assisted Natural Regeneration
8. Regions are working in selection of three National Forest Priority Areas for management plans preparation
9.The establishment of two botanical gardens is at its final stage
10. Scientific study on trade-offs and systems dynamics prepared
11 33 trainees are trained on urban greening at WGCF
12. 1 national guideline prepared for integration of green facilities in city planning</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">?	ToT provided for 35 experts and skill training provided for 1000 extension agents 
?	60 regional experts trained on forest governance
?	Forestry year book produced
?	85,000 hectars of dry forest properly managed
?	15,000 jobs created primarily for women and youth
?	one document produced for value chain and marketing of key forest products 
?	Three cooperatives established for key forest products</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">SLU and Wondo Genet College of Forestry (WGCF) provided one-month TOT training for 28 (5 women) senior regional 
experts and College teachers on three newly designed and skill-based modules (Forest extension, Agroforestry and Small-scale community forestry). The TOT training was given with 2 rounds for 28 trainees who constituted 80% of the target number .of trainees.
79,513 ha of dry forest is mapped and demarcated for PFM scheme
3,815 livelihood beneficiaries have been benefited through different livelihood activities.
 CIFOR is collecting frankincense samples to test processing and value addition technologies. EEFRI has also developed invitro propagation protocol for key multi-purpose species (Osyris quadripartita and Oxythenantera abyssinica).
 In Amhara region, 5 certified cooperatives with total members of 1310 are formed and one groups with total members of 28 is established and its certification process is underway.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Catalyzing project phase II proposal development
2. Exposure Visit for Phase II proposal development carried out
3. Ethiopian Statistical yearbook of forestry prepared and published
4.conduct development-oriented action research at landscape level
5. PFM to improve the management of dry forests including bamboo resources and link benefits with vulnerable livelihoods piloted
6 Establish permanent monitoring of landscapes to describe biodiversity and hydrology dynamics over time for various new production systems 
7. two botanical gardens establishment to enhance ex-situ biodiversity conservation finalized
8. tailored skill training for 20 (8 Female) experts/decision makers from the three pilot cities on urban green landscape design provided</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
